#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/kde/kf-apps/kdenlive.xml:96
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Kdenlive"
msgstr "Instalação do Kdenlive"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/kde/kf-apps/kdenlive.xml:99
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>Kdenlive</application> by running the following "
"commands:"
msgstr ""
"Instale <application>Kdenlive</application> executando os seguintes "
"comandos:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/kde/kf-apps/kdenlive.xml:103
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"cmake -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=$KF6_PREFIX \\\n"
"      -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release         \\\n"
"      -D BUILD_TESTING=OFF                \\\n"
"      -D FETCH_OTIO=ON                    \\\n"
"      -W no-dev .. &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"cmake -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=$KF6_PREFIX \\\n"
"      -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release         \\\n"
"      -D BUILD_TESTING=OFF                \\\n"
"      -D FETCH_OTIO=ON                    \\\n"
"      -W no-dev .. &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"

#.  renodr: I still don't like that we're doing this, but I know it's
#.            the best approach for BLFS 13.0
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/kde/kf-apps/kdenlive.xml:114
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The build process will download a Git repository of "
"<application>OpenTimelineIO</application>, totaling around 100 MB. "
"Configuration will seem to hang right after <command>cmake</command> begins "
"running. This is normal, it is fetching that Git repository. If it hangs for"
" a while, it's most likely due to a poor download speed during the download "
"process. The <parameter>-D FETCH_OTIO</parameter> CMake option should be "
"omitted if you have installed the <application>OpenTimelineIO</application> "
"package."
msgstr ""
"O processo de construção baixará um repositório Git do "
"<application>OpenTimelineIO</application>, totalizando cerca de 100 MB. A "
"configuração parecerá travar logo depois que o "
"<command>cmake</command>começar a executar. Isso é normal; ele está buscando"
" esse repositório Git. Se travar por um tempo, é muito provável que seja "
"devido a uma baixa velocidade de transferência durante o processo de "
"transferência. A opção do CMake <parameter>-D FETCH_OTIO</parameter> deveria"
" ser omitida se você tiver instalado o pacote "
"<application>OpenTimelineIO</application>."

